          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00007052555119504559,
          "sentence": "1. The two motivations behind the proposed approach—the need to understand the ambiguous use of words depending on context, and the need to generate new answers rather than just selecting from answers held by QA sites—are reasonable.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.999929474448805,
            "ai": 0.000050028017130560204,
            "paraphrased": 0.00002049753406448538
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00006813274023305701,
          "sentence": "2. The novelty in the paper involves the following: 1) incorporating biases of semantics behind questions into word embeddings using a paragraph2vec-like model, modified to take as inputs words from questions, a question title token, and a question category token; 2) modeling the optimal combination of sentences (conclusion and supplement sentences) in the predicted answer; 3) designing an abstract scenario for answers, inspired by the automated web-service composition framework (Rao & Su 2005); and 4) extracting important topics in the conclusion sentence and emphasizing them in the supplemental sentence using an attention mechanism (the attention mechanism is similar to Tan et al.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9999318672597669,
            "ai": 0.00004799765784024423,
            "paraphrased": 0.000020135082392812783
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0001257723261891968,
          "sentence": "2016).",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998742276738108,
            "ai": 0.0001076690088915413,
            "paraphrased": 0.000018103317297655482
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00010765023898497274,
          "sentence": "3. The proposed method is shown to outperform the current best method (Tan et al.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.999892349761015,
            "ai": 0.0000850639331496597,
            "paraphrased": 0.000022586305835313038
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
